# ============================================================================
# Topcat Worktops — articles/ only.
#
# ⛔ ONE LINE, AND THE LISTING PAGE DOES NOT WORK WITHOUT IT.
#
# `articles/` is a real directory at the web root, which no other hub on this
# site is. Apache's mod_dir sees it and 301s a request for /articles to
# /articles/ before any of the root .htaccess rules get a look in. That
# redirect is fatal rather than merely untidy: the rewrite that serves every
# clean URL on this host is guarded by `RewriteCond %{REQUEST_FILENAME} !-d`,
# and once the path has a trailing slash that test fails, so nothing answers.
# Directory indexing is refused on this box, so the visitor gets a 403.
#
# DirectorySlash Off stops that 301. The root .htaccess then answers /articles
# from the flat articles.html the export writes, and sends /articles/ back to
# the slash-less canonical form.
#
# It is scoped to this directory ON PURPOSE. Setting it at the web root would
# take the trailing slash away from /stones/, /guides/, /worktops/ and every
# other directory URL on the site, all of which depend on mod_dir adding it.
#
# ⚠️ DirectorySlash Off without a matching rule for the slash-less form would
# let Apache serve a directory listing. It cannot here — Options -Indexes is
# the host default and the root rules answer /articles first — but if this
# file is ever copied somewhere else, take that pairing with it.
# ============================================================================
DirectorySlash Off
